    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="0148" n="138" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg138"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/5–2247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-05-22">May 22,
                        1947</date>.<lb/>[Received May 22—5:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>108. Chinese military here informed me last night message from Changli reported
                    all Americans safe. Warner flew Tangshan this morning to phone mission Changli
                    and arrange their transportation Tientsin. Peitaiho reported quiet but about 20
                    persons including few Americans availing themselves Marine offer transportation
                    here from Chinwangtao. Two Americans already arrived here.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking as 94; repeated Department as 108 and Mukden, Peiping.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
